# An arriving answer supersedes ([LCRS.6.2.4]). Fixture 129_answer_supersede.
#
# Two Jobs fire `r` twice under `c1` before anything is answered. Then, all as
# host asserts:
#
#   ReplyA v=1, ReplyA v=2   the second withdraws the first (one live, v=2)
#   ReplyB v=3               another service's schema: ReplyA v=2 stays
#   Probe k=1, pump          logs `a 2 at 1`, `b 3 at 1`
#   CallError c1             withdraws ReplyA v=2 AND ReplyB v=3
#   Probe k=2, pump          logs only the CallError, for both Probes
#   ReplyB v=4               withdraws the CallError
#   Probe k=3, pump          logs `b 4` for all three Probes
#
# Each withdrawal is SUPERSEDED. Working memory loses the old answer before the
# new one enters, but the stream is input-first ([RFCS.6.7]): the answer's
# FactAssert, then its withdrawals.
# @spec [LCRS.6.2.4]
assert Job id=1
pump
assert Job id=2
pump
assert ReplyA corr="c1" v=1
assert ReplyA corr="c1" v=2
assert ReplyB corr="c1" v=3
assert Probe k=1
pump
assert CallError corr="c1" code="transport.timeout" message="late" ts=0
assert Probe k=2
pump
assert ReplyB corr="c1" v=4
assert Probe k=3
pump
